    "body": "In `GetPubKeyFromInput()`, extraction of public keys for `TxoutType::SCRIPTHASH` (P2SH-P2WPKH) inputs evaluates `txin.scriptSig` under `SCRIPT_VERIFY_NONE` and passes the resulting redeem script to `Solver(redeem, solutions)`.\n\nHowever, `Solver` starts by clearing `vSolutionsRet` (`solutions.clear()`). This discards the 20-byte P2SH script hash originally extracted from the UTXO's `scriptPubKey` without ever verifying that `Hash160(redeem)` matches it.\n\nBecause `GetPubKeyFromInput()` operates in isolation without full transaction script verification, an input spending any arbitrary P2SH UTXO (e.g. multisig, escrow, DLC) whose `scriptSig` evaluates to a valid P2WPKH script is erroneously identified as an eligible BIP-352 input. Its public key is extracted and added to A_sum, silently corrupting the input hash and the derived shared secret.\n\nAdditionally, `GetPubKeyFromInput()` did not enforce:\n1. `stack.size() == 1` after evaluating `txin.scriptSig` for `SCRIPTHASH` (ensuring BIP-16 single-element push).\n2. `Hash160(key) == solutions[0]` for both `WITNESS_V0_KEYHASH` and `SCRIPTHASH` (verifying that the extracted pubkey matches the 20-byte witness program).\n3. `txin.scriptWitness.stack.size() == 2` for standard P2WPKH witness stacks (`<sig> <pubkey>`).\n\n### Changes\n- Cache the expected 20-byte script hash before `Solver(redeem, solutions)` overwrites `solutions`.\n- Verify `stack.size() == 1` and `Hash160(stack.back()) == expected_script_hash`.\n- Enforce `txin.scriptWitness.stack.size() == 2` and check `Hash160(key) == solutions[0]` for both native P2WPKH and P2SH-P2WPKH inputs.\n- Add comprehensive unit tests in `src/test/bip352_tests.cpp` covering P2SH redeem script mismatch, single-push constraints, witness stack depths, and witness pubkey hash matching.",
