      ],
      "message": "bip352: verify redeem script and pubkey hash in GetPubKeyFromInput\n\nIn GetPubKeyFromInput, evaluating TxoutType::SCRIPTHASH (P2SH-P2WPKH) inputs\nruns EvalScript under SCRIPT_VERIFY_NONE and passes the resulting redeem script\nto Solver(redeem, solutions). However, Solver immediately clears the solutions\nvector, discarding the original 20-byte script hash from the UTXO's scriptPubKey\nwithout ever checking that Hash160(redeem) matches it.\n\nAs a result, any non-P2WPKH P2SH UTXO (e.g. multisig or timelock) spent by an input\nwhose scriptSig pushes a valid P2WPKH redeem script is mistakenly treated as an\neligible BIP-352 input, causing an unintended pubkey to be extracted and summed into\nA_sum, which silently corrupts the derived input_hash and shared secret.\n\nAdditionally, GetPubKeyFromInput fails to enforce:\n1. stack.size() == 1 for P2SH scriptSig (BIP-16 single-push constraint).\n2. Hash160(key) == solutions[0] (matching the witness program) for both\n   SCRIPTHASH and WITNESS_V0_KEYHASH.\n3. scriptWitness.stack.size() == 2 for standard P2WPKH witness stacks.\n\nFix this by:\n- Preserving the expected script hash before Solver(redeem, solutions) is invoked.\n- Verifying Hash160(redeem) == expected_script_hash.\n- Validating the witness stack size and ensuring Hash160(pubkey) matches the\n  target witness program for both P2WPKH and P2SH-P2WPKH.\n- Adding comprehensive unit tests covering P2SH redeem script mismatch, single-push\n  constraints, witness stack depths, and witness pubkey hash matching.",
